<h1>8. Design System</h1>

<h2>8.1 Colour Palette</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Role</th><th>Colour</th><th>Tailwind Class</th><th>Usage</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Background</td><td>#000000</td><td>bg-black</td><td>All page backgrounds</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Surface</td><td>#111827</td><td>bg-gray-900</td><td>Cards, inputs, modals</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Surface 2</td><td>#0a0a0f</td><td>bg-gray-950</td><td>Bottom sheets, deep cards</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Border</td><td>#374151</td><td>border-gray-700</td><td>Input borders, dividers</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Primary</td><td>#9333ea → #ec4899</td><td>from-purple-600 to-pink-600</td><td>CTA buttons, badges, gradients</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Accent Purple</td><td>#a855f7</td><td>text-purple-400</td><td>Links, active states, icons</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Text Primary</td><td>#ffffff</td><td>text-white</td><td>Headlines, important labels</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Text Secondary</td><td>#9ca3af</td><td>text-gray-400</td><td>Descriptions, metadata</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Text Muted</td><td>#4b5563</td><td>text-gray-600</td><td>Placeholder text, timestamps</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Success</td><td>#4ade80</td><td>text-green-400</td><td>Success states, active badges</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Error</td><td>#f87171</td><td>text-red-400</td><td>Error messages, warnings</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>8.2 Typography</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Font Family:</strong> System font stack (Calibri / Arial / sans-serif via Tailwind default)</li>
  <li><strong>Page Titles:</strong> 2xl–4xl, font-black or font-bold, text-white</li>
  <li><strong>Section Headers:</strong> xl–2xl, font-bold</li>
  <li><strong>Body Text:</strong> sm (14px), text-gray-300/400</li>
  <li><strong>Metadata:</strong> xs (12px), text-gray-500/600</li>
</ul>

<h2>8.3 Component Patterns</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Rounded corners:</strong> rounded-xl (12px) for cards, rounded-full for avatars/pills</li>
  <li><strong>CTA buttons:</strong> bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-600 to-pink-600, rounded-xl, font-bold</li>
  <li><strong>Input fields:</strong> bg-gray-900, border-gray-800, focus:border-purple-600, rounded-xl</li>
  <li><strong>Bottom sheets:</strong> Fixed bottom drawer, bg-gray-950, rounded-t-3xl, backdrop-blur</li>
  <li><strong>Sticky headers:</strong> bg-black/95, backdrop-blur-md, border-b border-gray-900</li>
  <li><strong>Cards:</strong> bg-gray-900/50, border border-gray-800, rounded-xl/2xl</li>
  <li><strong>Badges:</strong> Coloured pill spans with category-specific colours</li>
  <li><strong>Toasts:</strong> Fixed top-center, bg-gray-900, border-gray-700, rounded-2xl, 2.5s auto-dismiss</li>
</ul>

<!-- ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<h1>9. Context Providers &amp; State Management</h1>

<h2>9.1 UserContext</h2>
<p>Manages subscription tier and tab visibility. All child components can read <code>tier</code> (1, 2, or 3) to conditionally render tier-gated features. <code>tabVisibility</code> is a record mapping each <code>TabKey</code> to "Everyone" | "Friends" | "Hidden", controlling which profile tabs are visible to others.</p>

<h2>9.2 SocialContext</h2>
<p>Tracks the set of followed user IDs and the KliqStream "My List". Both are <code>Set&lt;string&gt;</code> values. <code>toggleFollow(userId)</code> and <code>toggleMyList(contentId)</code> are exposed to all components. KliqTube subscriptions use a <code>kt:</code> prefix on the user ID to avoid collision with social follows.</p>

<h2>9.3 NotificationContext</h2>
<p>Stores a list of notification objects (id, type, user, message, timestamp, avatar). <code>addNotification()</code> adds new items, <code>markRead()</code> clears the unread count. The Layout component reads <code>unreadCount</code> to show the live badge on both the desktop bell icon and the mobile Inbox nav button.</p>

<!-- ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<h1>10. Control System App Overview</h1>
<p>The KLIQ Control System (ctrl_1) is a separate web application running on port 5174, designed for platform administrators. It provides an operational view of the KLIQ platform with tools to manage users, moderate content, monitor analytics, send push notifications, and configure platform settings.</p>

<h2>10.1 Control Panel Pages</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Page</th><th>URL</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Dashboard</td><td>/</td><td>KPI overview, recent activity, system status, quick links to proto_3</td></tr>
  <tr><td>User Management</td><td>/users</td><td>Searchable user table with verify/suspend/ban actions</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Content Moderation</td><td>/content</td><td>Flagged content review with approve/reject workflows</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Communities</td><td>/communities</td><td>Community directory with feature/suspend controls</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Analytics</td><td>/analytics</td><td>Platform-wide charts for user growth, content, revenue</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Notifications</td><td>/notifications</td><td>Push notification composer with audience targeting</td></tr>
  <tr><td>App Settings</td><td>/settings</td><td>Feature flag toggles, platform configuration</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>10.2 Linking to proto_3</h2>
<p>The control panel links to the KLIQ app (proto_3, running on port 5173) in the following ways:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>"View App" button</strong> in the header opens proto_3 in a new tab</li>
  <li><strong>"View Profile" in Users table</strong> opens <code>localhost:5173/user/:username</code></li>
  <li><strong>"View Community" in Communities</strong> opens <code>localhost:5173/community/:id</code></li>
  <li><strong>"View Content" in Moderation</strong> links to the relevant watch/post page in proto_3</li>
</ul>

